preConditionHook:
// KAUFMAN'S EFFICIENCY RATIO: the net move over erLength bars divided by the
// total distance travelled to get there -- 0 for pure noise, 1 for an
// unbroken line. Identical both sides, because both terms are absolute.
// The source names it and gives neither a length nor a cutoff, so both are
// optimizer inputs; 10 is Kaufman's own default and 0.3 a starting
// threshold.
//
// No catalog rule measures net move against distance travelled --
// AdxBelowThreshold and the bar-overlap family read trendiness differently.
//
// epsilon guards the flat-market divide-by-zero, following
// CloseRangePosition: a zero denominator is a RUNTIME ERROR in EasyLanguage
// (VERIFIED), so epsilon must stay strictly positive in any grid.
//
// Differences only, no cross-bar state: the shift test passes and there is
// no EL variable history to mirror. Scratch is declared in localVariables,
// never at hook scope, so the rule survives double placement.
netMove = std::fabs(close[0] - close[(int)erLength]);
pathLen = 0.0;
for (ii = 0; ii < (int)erLength; ++ii) {
    pathLen = pathLen + std::fabs(close[ii] - close[ii + 1]);
}
